# Dashboard: Live TV logo treatment in rail cards & hero

## Context

Live TV channel logos look bad in the workspace dashboard. The screenshot in the original
request shows the "Recently Watched" rail rendering tiny channel logos (typically 100–256 px
square) inside a 172×258 px portrait card with `object-fit: cover`. Logos get upscaled and
crop-edged, producing the blurry "ZDF" / "WDR" tiles visible under *Zuletzt angesehen*. The
hero card (`Servus TV HD` in the screenshot) has the same defect.

VOD and series cards already look great because their poster artwork is large and
portrait-shaped. The fix is to render live-channel cards differently — keep card dimensions
identical so mixed-type rails stay uniform, but render the logo with `object-fit: contain` on
a blurred backdrop derived from the logo itself (the pattern used by Apple Podcasts hero
tiles and Plex Live TV channel cards).

User-confirmed direction:
- Contained logo + blurred backdrop ✅
- Keep current card width (172 px desktop / 140 px ≤720 px) ✅
- Apply same treatment to the hero ✅

## Approach

Add a `contentType` field to the rail/hero card models. The template branches on
`contentType === 'live'` to apply a `--live` modifier class. CSS handles all visual changes.
No layout reflow, no per-rail aspect-ratio changes, no behavioural changes for VOD/series.

## File-by-file changes

### 1. `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/dashboard-rail.component.ts`

Extend `DashboardRailCard` interface (line 28) with one optional field:

```typescript
export interface DashboardRailCard {
    id: string;
    title: string;
    subtitle?: string;
    imageUrl?: string;
    icon: string;
    contentType?: 'live' | 'movie' | 'series'; // NEW
    link: string[];
    state?: Record<string, unknown>;
    actions?: DashboardRailAction[];
}
```

### 2. `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/dashboard-rail.component.html`

Update the `.rail__art` block (lines 50–67) to:
1. Add a `[class.rail__art--live]` binding gated on `card.contentType === 'live'`.
2. Inject a `<span class="rail__art-bg">` element (positioned absolute) that holds the
   blurred backdrop, only when the live class is active and `card.imageUrl` exists.

```html
<div
    class="rail__art"
    [class.rail__art--live]="card.contentType === 'live'"
    [style.aspect-ratio]="aspectRatio()"
>
    @if (card.imageUrl && !failedImages()[card.id]) {
        @if (card.contentType === 'live') {
            <span
                class="rail__art-bg"
                aria-hidden="true"
                [style.background-image]="'url(' + card.imageUrl + ')'"
            ></span>
        }
        <img
            [src]="card.imageUrl"
            [alt]="card.title"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            (error)="markFailed(card.id)"
        />
    } @else {
        <div class="rail__art-fallback">
            <mat-icon>{{ card.icon }}</mat-icon>
        </div>
    }
</div>
```

### 3. `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/dashboard-rail.component.scss`

Append a new section after `.rail__art-fallback` (~line 253):

```scss
.rail__art--live {
    // Logo on a soft blurred-color backdrop derived from the logo itself.
    // Mirrors Apple Podcasts / Plex Live TV channel-tile treatment.
    img {
        object-fit: contain;
        padding: 18% 14%;
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
        // Subtle drop shadow lifts the logo off the blurred backdrop.
        filter: drop-shadow(0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35));
    }
}

.rail__art-bg {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    filter: blur(28px) saturate(1.4);
    transform: scale(1.4);
    opacity: 0.55;
    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
}
```

### 4. `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/workspace-dashboard-rails.component.ts`

Populate `contentType` on each card factory (lines 375–415):

```typescript
private toRecentCard(item: GlobalRecentItem): DashboardRailCard {
    return {
        // ...existing fields
        contentType: item.type,
    };
}

private toFavoriteCard(item: DashboardFavoriteItem): DashboardRailCard {
    return {
        // ...existing fields
        contentType: item.type,
    };
}

private toRecentlyAddedCard(item: DashboardRecentlyAddedItem): DashboardRailCard {
    return {
        // ...existing fields
        contentType: item.type,
    };
}
```

The `sourceCards` factory (lines 292–311) does not get `contentType` — playlist source
cards are not channel logos.

Add `contentType` to the hero model: locate `DashboardHeroModel` (defined in
`libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/...` — the `resolveDashboardHeroArtwork`
helper returns it; need to confirm exact file with a quick grep before editing). Add
`contentType: item.type` to the object returned at line 261.

### 5. `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/workspace-dashboard-rails.component.html`

Update the hero block (lines 46–114):

1. Add `[class.hero--live]="item.contentType === 'live'"` to the `<a class="hero">`.
2. Inside `.hero__poster` (lines 82–101), the existing `<img>` already covers — for live
   we want the logo contained. The blurred `.hero__backdrop` already exists (line 88), so
   for live we just need to override the poster image's fit.

```html
<a
    class="hero"
    data-test-id="dashboard-hero"
    [class.hero--with-image]="!!item.posterUrl || !!item.backdropUrl"
    [class.hero--has-backdrop]="item.hasBackdrop"
    [class.hero--has-default-backdrop]="item.backdropSource === 'fallback'"
    [class.hero--live]="item.contentType === 'live'"
    [routerLink]="item.link"
    [state]="item.state ?? {}"
>
```

### 6. `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/workspace-dashboard-rails.component.scss`

Append new rules after the `.hero__poster-fallback` block (~line 224):

```scss
.hero--live .hero__poster {
    img {
        object-fit: contain;
        padding: 14%;
        filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45));
    }
    // Soft tinted background derived from theme so the logo doesn't sit on a
    // dark void when the blurred backdrop image is light.
    background:
        radial-gradient(
            circle at 50% 35%,
            var(--app-selection-surface, rgba(120, 173, 255, 0.18)) 0%,
            transparent 65%
        ),
        var(--app-widget-bg, #1e2330);
}
```

The existing `.hero__backdrop` (the page-wide blurred wash) already provides the
ambient color — no extra backdrop element needed for the hero poster.

## Why this design

- **Single new field** (`contentType`) flows through existing card factories — type info is
  already available at every call site (`item.type`).
- **CSS-only visual change** — no template restructure, no breaking API change.
- **Mixed rails stay uniform**: VOD posters and live tiles share aspect ratio and width, so
  a "Recently Watched" rail with both types still aligns visually.
- **No regressions on VOD/series** — the `--live` class gates every new rule.
- **Fallback path unchanged**: when `imageUrl` is absent, the existing
  `rail__art-fallback` (centered `live_tv` Material icon) still renders. No work needed.

## Critical files

- `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/dashboard-rail.component.ts`
- `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/dashboard-rail.component.html`
- `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/dashboard-rail.component.scss`
- `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/workspace-dashboard-rails.component.ts`
- `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/workspace-dashboard-rails.component.html`
- `libs/workspace/dashboard/feature/src/lib/rails/workspace-dashboard-rails.component.scss`

## Open detail to confirm during implementation

Locate `DashboardHeroModel` definition (likely in a sibling `*.model.ts` or
`hero-artwork.ts` next to `resolveDashboardHeroArtwork`) and add the `contentType?` field
there before populating it from `item.type`. Quick `grep -r "DashboardHeroModel" libs/workspace/dashboard`
will pinpoint the file.

## Verification

1. Start Electron in dev mode:
   ```bash
   nx serve electron-backend
   ```

2. Use the user's Sender_DE_AT_News M3U playlist (or any M3U with live channel logos) and
   open the dashboard.

3. Visual checks:
   - Recently Watched rail: live channel cards (e.g., ZDF, WDR, Servus TV) show the **full
     logo**, centered, with breathing-room padding and a softly blurred color wash behind.
     No more cropped-edge upscaling.
   - VOD/Series cards in the same rail (if any) still show **full-bleed posters** —
     unchanged.
   - Hero card with a live channel: poster slot shows contained logo on a tinted backdrop,
     hero header backdrop wash unchanged.
   - Fallback (no `imageUrl`): live channels still render the `live_tv` icon centered on
     the existing radial-gradient fallback.

4. Use agent-browser to capture screenshots for before/after comparison:
   ```bash
   agent-browser --cdp 9222 screenshot /tmp/iptvnator-dashboard-after.png
   ```

5. Resize the viewport below 720 px to confirm the smaller-card breakpoint
   (`--rail-card-width: 140px`) still renders contained logos correctly.

6. Run lint and unit tests:
   ```bash
   nx lint workspace-dashboard-feature
   nx test workspace-dashboard-feature
   ```

7. Doc check: `apps/web/CLAUDE.md` and `docs/architecture/` do not document dashboard
